{"lemma":"חָרַשׁ","translit":"chârash","pronunciation":"khaw-rash'","def":"to scratch, i.e. (by implication) to engrave, plough; hence (from the use of tools) to fabricate (of any material); figuratively, to devise (in a bad sense); hence (from the idea of secrecy) to be silent, to let alone; hence (by implication) to be deaf (as an accompaniment of dumbness)","kjv":"[idiom] altogether, cease, conceal, be deaf, devise, ear, graven, imagine, leave off speaking, hold peace, plow(-er, man), be quiet, rest, practise secretly, keep silence, be silent, speak not a word, be still, hold tongue, worker.","occ":[[4,22,10,"Thou shalt not plow"],[16,4,14,"For if thou altogether"],[27,10,13,"Ye have plowed"],[22,28,24,"Doth the plowman"],[22,36,21,"But they held their peace"],[22,41,1,"Keep silence"],[17,13,13,"Hold your peace"],[17,41,12,"I will not conceal"],[19,3,29,"Devise"],[18,109,1,"Hold not thy peace"],[18,129,3,"The plowers"],[18,32,3,"When I kept silence"],[11,18,36,"held their peace"],[16,4,14,"holdest thy peace"],[22,28,24,"plow"],[17,11,3,"make"],[17,13,19,"with me? for now, if I hold my tongue"],[17,13,5,"ye would altogether"],[17,33,33,"unto me: hold thy peace"],[17,4,8,"they that plow"],[17,6,24,"me, and I will hold my tongue"],[6,18,19,"unto him, Hold thy peace"],[3,30,14,"altogether"],[19,14,22,"that devise"],[19,17,28,"when he holdeth his peace"],[19,20,4,"will not plow"],[19,6,18,"that deviseth"],[18,129,3,"plowed"],[18,50,21,"and I kept silence"],[1,14,14,"for you, and ye shall hold your peace"],[0,24,21,"at her held his peace"],[22,42,14,"I have been still"],[17,13,5,"hold your peace"],[32,3,12,"be plowed"],[3,30,11,"and held his peace"],[3,30,14,"hold his peace"],[3,30,7,"and held his peace"],[19,12,20,"of them that imagine"],[19,6,14,"he deviseth"],[18,35,22,"keep not silence"],[18,50,3,"and shall not keep silence"],[18,83,1,"hold not thy peace"],[8,23,9,"secretly practised"],[29,6,12,"plow"],[17,11,3,"hold their peace"],[17,33,31,"unto me: hold thy peace